```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Suspicious Scheduled Task Creation
# Detection ID: DE-PE-002
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1053.005 - Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task
# Data Source: Windows Security 4698 / Sysmon 1 (schtasks.exe)
# Severity: Medium
# ============================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4698
| rex field=TaskContent "(?i)<Command>(?P<task_command>[^<]+)</Command>"
| rex field=TaskContent "(?i)<Arguments>(?P<task_args>[^<]+)</Arguments>"
| where match(task_command,"(?i)(powershell|cmd|wscript|cscript|mshta|rundll32)") OR match(task_args,"(?i)(-enc|downloadstring|iex)")
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen values(task_command) as cmd values(task_args) as args by ComputerName, SubjectUserName, TaskName
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| sort -first_seen
```

## Detection Logic
Scheduled task creation events (4698) include the full task XML; extracting the Command/Arguments elements lets us flag tasks that launch interpreters or contain download-and-execute patterns, a common persistence and defense-evasion technique.

## False Positive Considerations
Patch management and backup software create scheduled tasks that call PowerShell for legitimate purposes — allowlist by TaskName prefix (e.g., 'Microsoft\\Windows\\UpdateOrchestrator').

## Tuning Notes
Requires 'Audit Other Object Access Events' enabled in Advanced Audit Policy; verify GPO coverage.
